                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "9a8d3fcc-2961-3055-bc41-54c943516a8b",
                        "entry_id": "e15795f9-16ba-375c-a623-9e09a61a367a",
                        "glosses": [
                            "связанный, соотносящийся по значению с существительным люстрин (рода ткани с глянцем)"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "f1cdbc44-ed66-3cc9-b4ac-6732116be449",
                        "entry_id": "e15795f9-16ba-375c-a623-9e09a61a367a",
                        "glosses": [
                            "сделанный, сшитый из люстрина"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "9fa8abe0-683d-410e-8c97-9383fecfc863",
                                "sense_id": "f1cdbc44-ed66-3cc9-b4ac-6732116be449",
                                "text": "«Кто бы это?» В ответ на этот вопрос в дверях является какой-то совершенно незнакомый гость; он торопливо сбрасывает с плеч полинялую люстриновую тальму, перекидывает её через руку и, остановившись перед хозяином, произносит: — Если не ошибаюсь, — господин Хрущов?"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b12b615c-eab9-430a-aeaf-6aa85abe4832",
                                "sense_id": "f1cdbc44-ed66-3cc9-b4ac-6732116be449",
                                "text": "Через пять минут на Ипполите Матвеевиче красовался лунный жилет, усыпанный мелкой серебряной звездой, и переливчатый люстриновый пиджачок."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "87938061-0ef1-4cd0-a681-ddccb353f965",
                        "source_entry_id": "e15795f9-16ba-375c-a623-9e09a61a367a",
                        "target_lang_word": "lustrine",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "lustrine",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b3b7f098-5233-3239-83a7-0738925eadd1",
                                        "entry_id": "35eac512-b8b9-3e5c-b5e1-f1675bdd4cad",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Alternative form of lustring."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "alt-of",
                                            "alternative"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "609d28ab-815c-482b-8c41-3f8348383a5a",
                        "source_entry_id": "e15795f9-16ba-375c-a623-9e09a61a367a",
                        "target_lang_word": "lutestring",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "lutestring",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "64a1767f-16cd-3e50-9ee8-2143580fc280",
                                        "entry_id": "24ba26cd-8bbc-3f5c-9197-63ad7d907a92",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A plain, stout, lustrous silk, used for ladies' dresses and for ribbon."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "archaic",
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8c58dad8-0f04-4309-9f7e-d8aec9a80bde",
                                                "sense_id": "64a1767f-16cd-3e50-9ee8-2143580fc280",
                                                "text": "There goes Mrs. Roundabout, I mean the fat lady in the luteſtring trollopee. Betvveen you and I, ſhe is but a cutler's vvife. See hovv ſhe's dreſſed, as fine as hands and pins can make her […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "55c9f987-8d44-4f4f-aba4-de6f944de346",
                                                "sense_id": "64a1767f-16cd-3e50-9ee8-2143580fc280",
                                                "text": "Lord, I have ſuch a deal to do, I ſhall ſcarce have time to ſlip on my Italian luteſting.—VVhere is this davvdle of a houſekeeper?"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4f1a3b57-96e9-431f-8a1e-098bdf74c879",
                                                "sense_id": "64a1767f-16cd-3e50-9ee8-2143580fc280",
                                                "text": "A dressing chemise of Tiffany which she had on over a blue lutestring"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "75ce9db2-449e-3fac-ae8b-3b417fad5832",
                                        "entry_id": "24ba26cd-8bbc-3f5c-9197-63ad7d907a92",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A type of moth with a band-like marking across the forewing, of the former taxonomic family Thyatiridae, also, the band-like marking."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "47d32764-310c-494d-9ab3-1d1fb3091f6e",
                                                "sense_id": "75ce9db2-449e-3fac-ae8b-3b417fad5832",
                                                "text": "There are six hook-tips and 10 in the lutestring group, which was formerly treated as a separate family, Thyatiridae."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "598ecc60-8385-46a6-9b64-482112714dc8",
                                                "sense_id": "75ce9db2-449e-3fac-ae8b-3b417fad5832",
                                                "text": "A quartet of moths in the subfamily Thyatirinae, known collectively as lutestrings – of which the spring-flying Frosted Green and Yellow Horned are also members."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "50b9f0cb-babc-473b-a7ed-474bfb204058",
                                                "sense_id": "75ce9db2-449e-3fac-ae8b-3b417fad5832",
                                                "text": "Other lutestrings (3 spp., each in its own genus [n/i]), which do not have black spot on forewing and lack the black dash on wingtip."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3238a81d-199e-48a8-9b02-efd9157138c9",
                                                "sense_id": "75ce9db2-449e-3fac-ae8b-3b417fad5832",
                                                "text": "These specimens have the \"lutestrings\" of or, and the \"figure of 80\" characteristic of octogessima."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e96cfbda-8b5d-3959-8e60-fdfd26848aca",
                                        "entry_id": "24ba26cd-8bbc-3f5c-9197-63ad7d907a92",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The string of a lute."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0a4db97c-9940-4ee0-8533-1af26afd8899",
                                                "sense_id": "e96cfbda-8b5d-3959-8e60-fdfd26848aca",
                                                "text": "More scrolls were wedged into the wall's pigeonholes, along with minature assemblages of circuitry and glass, a theramin wand, coils of lutestrings and ivory lute-keys, stacks of crystal discs, a broken gamelan."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9f76d0c3-b588-469d-9678-948dc7c79674",
                                                "sense_id": "e96cfbda-8b5d-3959-8e60-fdfd26848aca",
                                                "text": "Seventeen shillings went on replacement lutestrings for Elizabeth herself. Her greatest pleasures were playing her lute or virginals, reading or sewing."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5a164265-6ebf-4ab9-bc58-ee651edb3786",
                                                "sense_id": "e96cfbda-8b5d-3959-8e60-fdfd26848aca",
                                                "text": "When, I say, that the motion of an Object is imprest upon a Corporeal Organ, I would not have it understood that the motion, for example, of the Eye is only made there, but that it passess up to the Brain, from whence the Fibres of the Nerves, like Lutestrings in a Lute, are stretcht out to other Members."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "dba31389-5b16-409d-858b-e1eb0e9beff7",
                                                "sense_id": "e96cfbda-8b5d-3959-8e60-fdfd26848aca",
                                                "text": "Wondering how else he passed his time, Winifred surveyed the room again, this time without regard for the monetary value of the things she saw. A box of lutestrings. Five songbooks. But no lute."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8b5907ff-fae0-42a0-b146-d17a80bdb285",
                                                "sense_id": "e96cfbda-8b5d-3959-8e60-fdfd26848aca",
                                                "text": "Henry VIII. and his daughters Mary and Elizabeth are said to have been good lutenists. The smaller gut strings, called by the pleasant name of minnikins, were easily broken, and a gift of lutestrings was considered a present fit for a queen, and one which the great Elizabeth did not disdain."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "82817bc2-54f0-425f-9c24-5fadd5d53cd7",
                        "source_entry_id": "e15795f9-16ba-375c-a623-9e09a61a367a",
                        "target_lang_word": "lustrine",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "lustrine",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2ac46bc7-a9fb-3f48-9fa4-0f572de0ddfd",
                                        "entry_id": "7a14a840-4193-304d-8ca2-06006ef1ded6",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Étoffe de coton utilisée en confection, fortement apprêtée et lustrée ce qui lui donne beaucoup de brillant."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bcb1474f-d21a-41c9-bf4f-d52ba49ddfed",
                                                "sense_id": "2ac46bc7-a9fb-3f48-9fa4-0f572de0ddfd",
                                                "text": "Une doublure de lustrine."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d94d853a-accd-4a2a-b0bc-58f11c659b57",
                                                "sense_id": "2ac46bc7-a9fb-3f48-9fa4-0f572de0ddfd",
                                                "text": "L'atmosphère alourdie par le poêle, le pupitre usé par les coudes, le fauteuil à rond de cuir, la manchette de lustrine qu'on passe sur l'habit."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5a8a5d8a-4c56-4abd-95be-193e40db3164",
                                                "sense_id": "2ac46bc7-a9fb-3f48-9fa4-0f572de0ddfd",
                                                "text": "Les ouvrières qui restaient encore défirent leurs manchettes de lustrine, se lissèrent les cheveux avec du crachat."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b862c3a7-424a-4306-bc4b-47f6d6d06149",
                                                "sense_id": "2ac46bc7-a9fb-3f48-9fa4-0f572de0ddfd",
                                                "text": "Le détective disparut derrière la tenture de lustrine au moment où la porte du bureau fut ouverte sans ménagement."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8e7b2641-e496-43ef-b239-5420c684c056",
                                                "sense_id": "2ac46bc7-a9fb-3f48-9fa4-0f572de0ddfd",
                                                "text": "Ma mère termina, grâce à la machine à coudre, une blouse noire d’écolier, taillée dans une craquante lustrine, qui brillait de tout son apprêt : je ne devais plus la porter dans la rue, mais seulement au lycée, d’où elle ne sortirait pas."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f45dbc79-f14c-434e-a426-8218a4de6dc2",
                                                "sense_id": "2ac46bc7-a9fb-3f48-9fa4-0f572de0ddfd",
                                                "text": "Les quelques sièges disparaissaient sous des housses. Même le lustre était enveloppé de lustrine."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "85a12d7a-3324-4345-a367-89df322af3b7",
                                                "sense_id": "2ac46bc7-a9fb-3f48-9fa4-0f572de0ddfd",
                                                "text": "L’ennemi n’est plus seulement reconnaissable à ses uniformes vert-de-gris, à ses longs imperméables, il peut aussi se dissimuler sous les manches de lustrine des employés de mairie, sous la pèlerine des sergents de ville, sous l’autorité des préfets et jusque dans le regard amical des voisins."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "48ccbb42-8149-32ab-b39f-1ac6a924ce22",
                                        "entry_id": "7a14a840-4193-304d-8ca2-06006ef1ded6",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Manche de lustrine."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "ellipsis"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6c0ab995-0f2c-4ed4-a195-34f0e8466e44",
                                                "sense_id": "48ccbb42-8149-32ab-b39f-1ac6a924ce22",
                                                "text": "Enfin j’enfonce mes bras dans les petites manches de lustrine verte que maman m’a cousues de ses mains, et j’attends mes élèves…"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2fa689ad-c6fa-48ba-8821-a684047ff95f",
                                                "sense_id": "48ccbb42-8149-32ab-b39f-1ac6a924ce22",
                                                "text": "Optez pour une banque sans guichets et avec moins d'administratifs à lustrine qui prennent des airs."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7fee0891-9cc7-479a-ae58-014cd53d7358",
                                                "sense_id": "48ccbb42-8149-32ab-b39f-1ac6a924ce22",
                                                "text": "Son col de linge frais repassé, sa robe noire unie appelaient l’accompagnement de la paire de manches en lustrine, attribut des anciens scribes."
                                            }
